Task 2: Monitor Traffic Between Services
Subtask 2.1: Deploy Sample Application
Let's deploy a sample microservices application to generate traffic for monitoring.

# Create a namespace for our sample application
kubectl create namespace bookinfo

# Label the namespace for Istio injection
kubectl label namespace bookinfo istio-injection=enabled

# Deploy the Bookinfo sample application
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.19/samples/bookinfo/platform/kube/bookinfo.yaml -n bookinfo

# Verify deployment
kubectl get pods -n bookinfo
Wait for all pods to be in Running status before proceeding.

Subtask 2.2: Create Istio Gateway and VirtualService
# Apply Istio gateway configuration
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/istio/istio/release-1.19/samples/bookinfo/networking/bookinfo-gateway.yaml -n bookinfo

# Verify gateway creation
kubectl get gateway -n bookinfo
kubectl get virtualservice -n bookinfo
Subtask 2.3: Generate Application Traffic
Create a script to generate continuous traffic to our application:

# Create traffic generation script
cat << 'EOF' > generate_traffic.sh
#!/bin/bash

# Get the ingress gateway external IP
INGRESS_HOST=$(kubectl get po -l istio=ingressgateway -n istio-system -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.hostIP}')
INGRESS_PORT=$(kubectl -n istio-system get service istio-ingressgateway -o jsonpath='{.spec.ports[?(@.name=="http2")].nodePort}')
GATEWAY_URL=$INGRESS_HOST:$INGRESS_PORT

echo "Generating traffic to: http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage"

# Generate traffic in a loop
for i in {1..100}; do
    curl -s "http://$GATEWAY_URL/productpage" > /dev/null
    echo "Request $i sent"
    sleep 2
done
EOF

# Make script executable
chmod +x generate_traffic.sh

# Run traffic generation in background
./generate_traffic.sh &
